Step 0 supports a viable Track B family, but not the naïve “output the hemisystem” proposal: even the smallest \(p=5\) hemisystem has 378 lines, already beyond the 256-atom cap. I’m instead using Proposition 4.8 and Appendix A, which are part of the construction’s orbit-selection machinery. They turn a costly exact exponentiation in \(\mathbb F_{p^2}\) into a residue-class invariant modulo 16. The generator will compose many independently transformed copies, keeping the witness compact while making blind branch-guessing exponentially unlikely.
