The entire easy panel solved, and the medium rung is also being solved so far. Increasing prime size only raises the mechanical arithmetic cost; it does not hide the invariant once recognized. I’ll let the mandated ladder reach its own verdict—`hardened`, `cap_bound`, or `too_easy`—rather than reinterpret these successes.
