The bare loop has now genuinely held at `(n=63, k=48)`: all three exact answers were wrong, with valid parsing and no API errors. Before accepting that rung, I’m correcting two audit issues in the draft: G4 must sample the deducible two-branch space (`2^k`), not the naïve full field, and G7 must test a doubled batch because 63-bit deterministic primality is the module’s bit-size ceiling.
